  "Question": "Given point \\(A(-2,3)\\), point \\(B\\) is the reflection of \\(A\\) across the \\(x\\)-axis, and point \\(C\\) is the reflection of \\(A\\) across the \\(y\\)-axis. Find the area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "12",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(B(-2,-3)\\) and \\(C(2,3)\\). \\(AB\\) is perpendicular to the \\(x\\)-axis and has length 6; \\(AC\\) is parallel to the \\(x\\)-axis and has length 4. Since \\(\\angle A=90^\\circ\\), the area is \\(6\\times4\\div2=12\\).",
